  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0051_add537193c65.jpg\" style=\"height: 141px; width: 200px;\" /><br /><br />As we are are moving away from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> toward sheet <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> spacing between electric lines of force is increasing. <math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>∴</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></msub></math> In direction of electric field potential decreases. <math><mo>∴</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> </mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></msub></math>"
